  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an integer array `nums`, output *the most frequent even element*.\n\nIf there is a tie, output the **smallest** one. If there is no such element, output `-1`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [0,1,2,2,4,4,1]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\nThe even elements are 0, 2, and 4. Of these, 2 and 4 appear the most.\nWe return the smallest one, which is 2.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [4,4,4,9,2,4]\nOutput: 4\nExplanation: 4 is the even element appears the most.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [29,47,21,41,13,37,25,7]\nOutput: -1\nExplanation: There is no even element.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 2000`\n* `0 <= nums[i] <= 105`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
